---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getRoll } from '../lib/photos';

const roll = await getRoll();
const count = roll.length;
---

<Base title="About" compact>
  <section class="about">
    <h1>On waiting for weather.</h1>
    <p>
      Jamm photographs quiet places — coastlines at the turn of the tide, fog that
      arrives without warning, fields that go on longer than they should. The work is
      less about the subject than the light that happens to be passing through it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Everything here is shot on a small set of cameras and left mostly alone
      afterwards. No drama, no rescue in the edit. If a frame needed saving, it didn't
      make the roll.
    </p>

    <dl class="colophon">
      <div>
        <dt>Frames</dt>
        <dd>{count} on the current roll</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Working with</dt>
        <dd>Film &amp; medium format, mostly</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Set in</dt>
        <dd>Spectral &amp; Space Mono</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Built with</dt>
        <dd><a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a></dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Contact</dt>
        <dd><a href="mailto:hello@jamm.photography">hello@jamm.photography</a></dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>
</Base>
